-- title:
--   Section at ∞ of the two-chart model of X₁(Mp)
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((q))$ (Laurent series over $L$) which equals $L$-adjoined to the image, under the coefficientwise map $\mathbb{Q}((q)) \to L((q))$ induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, of the field [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p)`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L137) of $q$-expansions attached to $\Gamma_1(Mp)$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with an algebra structure over which $L$ is its fraction field, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A \to L$; assume $A$ acts on $K$ compatibly with $A \to L \to K$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with image in $L((q))$ the coefficientwise image of the Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the $j$-invariant numerator power series over $\mathbb{Q}$. Then the set of morphisms $\varphi \colon \operatorname{Spec} A \to \mathrm{TwoChartModel}(A,K,j)$ — the pushout gluing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $A$-subalgebras of $K$ generated by $j$ and by $j^{-1}$ — with $\varphi$ followed by the structure morphism [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) equal to $\mathrm{id}_{\operatorname{Spec} A}$ is nonempty.
--
--   The section produced is the cusp $\infty$, rational over $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$ and visible on the pole chart through the augmentation sending $1/j$ to $0$; it provides the rigidifying section of the structure morphism of the integral two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$. It is obtained from the general criterion producing such a section from an $A$-algebra homomorphism out of the pole-chart algebra, transported along the identification of the two descriptions of the two-chart model, and it is used in the count of points of the special fibre.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOneP_nonempty_schemeHomOver_id_modelTo_twoChartModel_x1_mul.lean

